     6	| Status | Shipped              |
     7	
     8	The tool registry is the boundary between model-produced calls and application executors, so it owns checking the schema that providers receive for each tool.
     9	
    10	## Execution
    11	
    12	The registry validates each input against the resolved tool definition's JSON Schema before the executor runs. A rejected call returns a `ToolResponse` describing its failing required field or type without including submitted values; the executor is not called. Schema-valid unknown properties are forwarded unchanged and only one executor invocation occurs ([validated by: returns a required-field rejection before invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L14), [rejects a wrong-typed value without exposing it and forwards valid extra keys unchanged once](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L30)).
    13	
    14	## Schema lifetime
    15	
    16	A function-valued definition is resolved and validated against the schema it returns for that execution, while an invalid static definition fails during registration and identifies the tool that could not be registered ([validated by: uses the schema currently returned by a definition source on every execution](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L54), [rejects an uncompilable static schema at registration time and names its tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).

